                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Salt Lake City UT",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued August 31 at 9:44PM MDT until August 31 at 11:45PM MDT by NWS Salt Lake City UT",
                "description": "FFWSLC\n\nThe National Weather Service in Salt Lake City has extended the\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nCentral Garfield County in southern Utah...\n\n* Until 1145 PM MDT.\n\n* At 944 PM MDT, the gauge on the Escalante River at Escalante is\nstill reporting flows in excess of 2000 cfs, leading to high flows\nwithin the Upper Escalante River Canyon. These high flows stem from\nearlier heavy rainfall from thunderstorms. Flash flooding is\nalready occurring.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Gauge reported.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks, streams, slot\ncanyons, and normally dry washes.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nPine Creek Box Canyon and Upper Escalante River Canyon.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nMove to higher ground now. Act quickly to protect your life.\n\nRemain alert for flooding even in locations not receiving rain. Dry\nwashes, streams, and rivers can become raging killer currents in a\nmatter of minutes, even from distant rainfall.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
